==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Black Knight Kyklops''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Demon Knight Kyklops''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
White Knight Cyclops is a thoroughly underwhelming backliner who suffers from below average DPS, high cost and long recharge time, with all of their other stats being painfully average aside from their higher than normal movement speed. Multi-hit divides their attack power into two equally strong hits and may cause them to only deal half damage to enemies that are easily knocked back, further hampering their general use. The lack of Surge Immunity also greatly hurts their utility. This leads to him being outclassed easily by countless superior alternatives.

Like most Dark Heroes, Cyclops' stats don't improve between forms, with each form instead having different abilities and ostensibly acting as sidegrades to one another.

==='''Normal Form'''===
White Knight Cyclops in their normal form has a 50% chance to freeze Aliens and Aku as well as a 50% chance to pierce shields, which seems promising in theory but utterly falls flat in practice, because they only activate on his first hit, and his very long attack cycle further reduces its consistency/potential uptime. For Aliens, he is completely outclassed by Seafarer Cat, who has a much faster attack cycle and a higher Freeze chance, whereas Aku enemies possess Shields which block status effect, as getting both a Shield Pierce and the Freeze on the same hit is rather unlikely.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Black Knight Kyklops trades the Freeze and Shield Pierce of their normal form for Strong Against and Immune to Waves. This raises their stats to workable levels against Aliens and Aku, but they are still on the lower end compared to other Ubers targeting the same traits. Notably, they are much less likely to be folded in an instant by Death Surges, and their Wave Immunity improves their matchups against the likes of [[Youcan]] and [[Deathkory]]. While they no longer have shield pierce to deal with Aku, its own Shield Piercing was already horrendous to begin with and isn't too much of a trade-off. Strong UP combos should be considered to get the most out of Kyklops, and are easy to justify if you are also using [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] and/or Talented [[Li'l Fish Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Island Cat]].

Due to their poor base stats, this unit should not be used as an anti-Wave generalist like Talented [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]] or even [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Awakened Musashi]].

==='''True Form'''===
Demon Knight Kyklops trades the defense fortifying Strong Against and Wave Immunity of their evolved form - as well as their Alien target - in favor of Massive Damage against Aku, regains their 50% Shield Pierce Chance, and also has Freeze Immunity. Most of what was written about their normal form still applies to their true form, except now they'll be able to deal a good amount of damage against Aku before getting sniped by a surge attack. Demon Knight Kyklops's heightened damage and multi-hit does open up the greater possibility of brute forcing an Aku shield with the first hit and damaging them directly with the second, but without Catseyes there are few shields they could break with a single hit. In terms of Freeze Immunity, the wide variety of superior Freeze Immune attackers immediately invalidate his presence, and while some Aku threats do abuse it, Demon Knight Kyclops proves to be a poor matchup against them all. [[Cerberus Kids]], while threatening if they do get the hit, are peons with practically no relevance otherwise. Meanwhile, despite his high range, he can be easily sniped by [[Wicked Face]], [[Ackey]], [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] and [[Omens]] as he cannot outrange them, their LD attacks or their Waves/Surges.

Additionally, Demon Knight Kyklops gains a 1-slot Massive Damage UP (Sm) Cat Combo, boosting damage of all units with this ability by 10% against their target traits. While combos boosting direct damage tend to be much more reliable and consistent for all units, it still has a point in its favor from time to time, given it takes only one slot and boosts the unit included within.

==='''Talents'''===
Kyklops' Talents are interesting, as he regains a prior ability that his 2nd form has.

'''[[Strengthen]]''' doubles his damage when maxed out, greatly improving his DPS and therefore has maximum priority. Because he has three Knockbacks and it activates on the first, he can still reposition once and deliver heavy damage for quite a while.

'''[[Special Abilities#Immune To Waves|Wave Immunity]]''' is carried over from his 2nd form, which makes his matchups against certain enemies, especially [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave Enemies]] a lot more favorable. Namely, he becomes a viable counter to [[Deathkory]] and [[Wicked Face]], although the latter still outranges him. Definitely not a bad Talent to have for its cost.

'''Cost Down''' is generally the least worthwhile of his Talents. Despite the massive cost reduction he incurs, his price tag was never much of an issue to begin with. This sort of quality of life typically isn't worth the 175 NP you'll spend on it, unless you're intending to hyper-invest into him.

'''Stat Talents''' are amazing for his role as an Anti-[[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] attacker, and synergize very well with his Strengthen Talent.

